From 2f8ce110c231353dd29d887b58d58380bbe09bc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 21:30:07 -0700
Subject: cranelift/pulley: fuse brif + 2 xloads at call_indirect dispatch tail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the new Pulley `xfuncref_dispatch_*` ops (two commits back)
into the Cranelift Pulley backend. At call_indirect lazy-init brif
sites where (a) `is_eagerly_initialized_funcref_table` holds AND
(b) the sig check is statically elided (typed-funcref table or
matching-sig-cache hit), the brif + the two VMFuncRef field loads
emitted by `load_code_and_vmctx` are fused into one
`MInst::FuncrefDispatch` whose underlying bytecode is one of the
four `xfuncref_dispatch_*` variants. Saves 2 match_loop dispatches
per call_indirect site.

Layered changes:

  pulley_shared::inst: new `MInst::FuncrefDispatch` terminator
  variant with `dst_code / dst_vmctx / src / offset_code /
  offset_vmctx / size / taken / not_taken`. Treated as a Branch by
  `is_term`; the operand collector reports both dsts as defs and
  src as a use, so regalloc handles the cross-block live ranges
  (FuncrefDispatch is emitted in the predecessor block; the dsts'
  uses live across the branch into the continuation).

  pulley_shared::lower::pre_lower: backend pre-pass that scans every
  block for the canonical pattern (brif of band(v, -2), where the
  taken target is a block whose first two CLIF insts are loads from
  the brif's first block-call-arg at the canonical
  `vm_func_ref_wasm_call` / `vm_func_ref_vmctx` offsets). When
  matched, the two continuation-block loads are marked
  `sink_pure_inst`. The band is NOT sunk — its result vreg is
  consumed as FuncrefDispatch's `src`.

  pulley_shared::lower::try_fuse_funcref_dispatch: per-brif
  recogniser in `lower_branch`. Re-derives the pattern (matched
  the same way as the pre-pass), looks up the relevant vregs, emits
  one FuncrefDispatch MachInst, and returns true. Phase-1's
  `try_fuse_band_brif` is tried only as a fallback when phase 2
  does NOT match, so on workloads where the eager-init + sig-elide
  pattern fires every time, phase 1's BandBrIf ops never appear in
  the final bytecode. (Phase 1's infrastructure — sink_pure_inst,
  the mask = -2 gate, the `MInst::BandBrIf` op — remains for the
  fallback case and for clarity of the layered design.)

  pulley_shared::inst::emit: `FuncrefDispatch` emits as a forward
  `xfuncref_dispatch_x{32,64}` followed by an unconditional jump to
  not_taken, with the inverted `xfuncref_dispatch_not_*` encoded
  into the `add_cond_branch` slot for MachBuffer fallthrough
  optimization. Same scaffolding as `MInst::BrIf` and
  `MInst::BandBrIf`.

Tests:

  tests/disas/pulley-call-indirect-band-brif-fusion.wat: re-blessed.
  The dispatch tail is now `xband64_s8 ; xfuncref_dispatch_not_x64 ;
  call_indirect` — three Pulley ops instead of the unfused five.
  The standalone xload64le's for the wasm_call / vmctx fields are
  gone, as is the standalone br_if.

  Disas + table_mutability suites: 2228 + 16, all pass.
